+**Resequenced 2026-08-10 — cache and image now precede cutover.** The original
+order put P2 cutover ahead of the cache and AMI work. That order regresses
+heavy-lane wall time. The manual burst workers are non-ephemeral: they serve
+many jobs across their TTL and accumulate a warm Turbo cache, a warm bun store,
+and a reused checkout. One-job-one-VM discards all of it on every job, so
+cutting over before a remote cache exists means every heavy job starts cold.
+The security and cost wins are real, but they would land alongside a speed
+loss. Cache and image are therefore prerequisites of cutover, not its sequel.
